    "Encourage breastfeeding mothers to pump their milk and store. Fluids by mouth may contraindicated because of tachypnea, weakness, and fatigue. IV fluids are preferred. Nasogastric fluids may be required",
    "If Children admitted to the hospital: separate rooms or cohort with similar infection, Contact and Standard Precautions used, Hand washing to reduce spread of the illness.",
